<node id="Evidence::Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_14">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_14</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 7, Equation (6)</data>
  <data key="d7">Under this condition the following model is proposed: K = at^b [Cl]^c (W/D)^d where K = mass loss; a, b, c and d = constants; [Cl] = chloride deposition rate; W = rainfall (mm); D = rainy days; t = time of exposure.</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 7, Equation (6)</data>
</node>
<node id="Expression::Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::expr_15">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::expr_15</data>
  <data key="d2">K = 18.8516t^{1.0947} [Cl]^{0.4313} [w/D]^{-0.2447}</data>
  <data key="d5">K = 18.8516t^{1.0947} [Cl]^{0.4313} [w/D]^{-0.2447}</data>
  <data key="d6">Regression analysis for steel mass loss (K) as a power law function of time (t), chloride deposition rate ([Cl]), rainfall amount (w), and number of rainy days (D).</data>
</node>
