  <data key="d2">[Cl] – 0.41W</data>
  <data key="d6">Rainfall (W) diminishes the mass loss caused by chloride ions ([Cl]) for steel.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_cpl_150641257">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_cpl_150641257</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 6, Equation (3) and surrounding text</data>
  <data key="d7">This regression equation shows that the influence of rainfall is important in determining mass loss of steel in the presence of chloride ions and that while washing effect of rain increases, mass loss diminishes.</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 6, Equation (3) and surrounding text</data>
</node>
<node id="Coupling::Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::cpl_108962036">
  <data key="d0">Coupling</data>
  <data key="d1">Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::cpl_108962036</data>
  <data key="d2">[Cl] – 0.016W</data>
  <data key="d6">Rainfall (W) diminishes the mass loss caused by chloride ions ([Cl]) for copper.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_cpl_366898794">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_cpl_366898794</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 7, Equation (4) and surrounding text</data>
  <data key="d7">This result confirms the influence of rainfall in diminishing mass loss due to the effect of chloride ions.</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 7, Equation (4) and surrounding text</data>
</node>
<node id="Coupling::Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::cpl_51091231">
  <data key="d0">Coupling</data>
  <data key="d1">Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::cpl_51091231</data>
  <data key="d2">[Cl]^c (W/D)^d</data>
  <data key="d6">The washing effect of rain (W/D) interacts with and affects the influence of chloride deposition rate ([Cl]) on corrosion.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_cpl_857082003">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_cpl_857082003</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 7, Equation (6) and surrounding text</data>
  <data key="d7">This washing effect could affect the influence of chloride deposition rate on corrosion.</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 7, Equation (6) and surrounding text</data>
</node>
<node id="Coupling::Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::cpl_620703881">
  <data key="d0">Coupling</data>
  <data key="d1">Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::cpl_620703881</data>
  <data key="d2">[Cl]^{0.4313} [w/D]^{-0.2447}</data>
  <data key="d6">The influence of chloride ions ([Cl]) on steel mass loss is strongly related to the rain regime (w/D), where increased rain regime reduces corrosion.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_cpl_188648473">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_cpl_188648473</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 8, Equation (7) and surrounding text</data>
  <data key="d7">It means that the factors selected represent correctly the behaviour of steel in atmospheric conditions, that is, the influence of chloride ions is strongly related to the rain regime.</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 8, Equation (7) and surrounding text</data>
</node>
<node id="Coupling::Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::cpl_772730395">
  <data key="d0">Coupling</data>
  <data key="d1">Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::cpl_772730395</data>
  <data key="d2">[Cl]^{0.2616} [w/D]^{-0.2379}</data>
  <data key="d6">The complex chloride deposition rate-rain regime (w/D) is important for determining copper mass loss, where increased rain regime reduces corrosion.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_cpl_218291058">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">Changes in atmospheric corrosion rate caused by chloride ions depending on rain regime.pdf::ev_cpl_218291058</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 8, Equation (9) and surrounding text</data>
  <data key="d7">It confirms that the complex chloride deposition rate-rain regime is important for determining mass loss of copper and steel.</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 8, Equation (9) and surrounding text</data>
</node>
