</node>
<node id="Coupling::09CuPCrNi_Weatherability_Tropical_Marine_Environment.pdf::cpl_433587042">
  <data key="d0">Coupling</data>
  <data key="d1">09CuPCrNi_Weatherability_Tropical_Marine_Environment.pdf::cpl_433587042</data>
  <data key="d2">Chloride ion and Cr together influence weatherability; when chloride deposition is high, Cr's effect is impaired, and chloride ion plays a significant role. Conversely, with low chloride deposition, Cr remarkably improves weatherability.</data>
  <data key="d6">Chloride ion and Cr together influence weatherability; when chloride deposition is high, Cr's effect is impaired, and chloride ion plays a significant role. Conversely, with low chloride deposition, Cr remarkably improves weatherability.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::09CuPCrNi_Weatherability_Tropical_Marine_Environment.pdf::ev_cpl_915190473">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">09CuPCrNi_Weatherability_Tropical_Marine_Environment.pdf::ev_cpl_915190473</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 7, Section 4.4</data>
  <data key="d7">It is reasonably inferred that chloride ion and Cr together influence weatherability; when the amount of chloride ion deposition reaches some level...the effect of Cr is impaired</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 7, Section 4.4</data>
</node>
