<node id="Expression::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_58">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_58</data>
  <data key="d2">AF(T) = e^{B(1/To - 1/T)}</data>
  <data key="d5">AF(T) = e^{B(1/To - 1/T)}</data>
  <data key="d6">Arrhenius model for acceleration factor due to temperature.</data>
</node>
<node id="OperatorFamily::INV_T">
  <data key="d0">OperatorFamily</data>
  <data key="d1">INV_T</data>
  <data key="d2">INV_T</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_58">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_58</data>
  <data key="d2">p. 5, Eq 4</data>
  <data key="d7">the effect of temperature on the corrosion process can be described by the Arrhenius model (Escobar and Meeker 2006), which is AF(T) = e^(B(1/To - 1/T))</data>
  <data key="d8">p. 5, Eq 4</data>
</node>
<node id="Expression::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_59">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_59</data>
  <data key="d2">f(T) = \begin{cases} 0.062(T-10) &amp; T&lt;10 \\ -0.021(T-10) &amp; T&gt;10 \end{cases}</data>
  <data key="d5">f(T) = \begin{cases} 0.062(T-10) &amp; T&lt;10 \\ -0.021(T-10) &amp; T&gt;10 \end{cases}</data>
  <data key="d6">Temperature function for zinc corrosion model.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_59">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_59</data>
  <data key="d2">p. 12, Table 1, Kucera et al. 2007 model</data>
  <data key="d7">This model is built for zinc. Models for carbon steel, copper, bronze, and limestone can be referred in Ref. (Kucera et al. 2007).</data>
  <data key="d8">p. 12, Table 1, Kucera et al. 2007 model</data>
</node>
<node id="Expression::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_60">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_60</data>
  <data key="d2">\xi = a \cdot \exp(-Ea/RT) \cdot \exp(\gamma \cdot RH) \cdot \exp(\eta\cdot SO_2) \cdot \exp(\lambda\cdot Cl)</data>
  <data key="d5">\xi = a \cdot \exp(-Ea/RT) \cdot \exp(\gamma \cdot RH) \cdot \exp(\eta\cdot SO_2) \cdot \exp(\lambda\cdot Cl)</data>
  <data key="d6">Generalized Eyring model for corrosion effect.</data>
</node>
<node id="OperatorFamily::ARRHENIUS">
  <data key="d0">OperatorFamily</data>
  <data key="d1">ARRHENIUS</data>
  <data key="d2">ARRHENIUS</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_60">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_60</data>
  <data key="d2">p. 14, Eq 18</data>
  <data key="d7">The generalized Eyring model also doesn't consider the interactive effects between various environmental factors. The model follows</data>
  <data key="d8">p. 14, Eq 18</data>
</node>
<node id="Expression::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_61">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_61</data>
  <data key="d2">\xi = a \cdot \exp (\beta\cdot T + y \cdot RH + \eta \cdot SO_2 + \lambda \cdot Cl)</data>
  <data key="d5">\xi = a \cdot \exp (\beta\cdot T + y \cdot RH + \eta \cdot SO_2 + \lambda \cdot Cl)</data>
  <data key="d6">Generalized log-linear model for corrosion effect.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_61">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_61</data>
  <data key="d2">p. 14, Eq 19</data>
  <data key="d7">The generalized log-linear model is a simple logarithmic model which follows \xi = a · exp (β· T + y · RH + η · SO2 + λ · Cl)</data>
  <data key="d8">p. 14, Eq 19</data>
</node>
