<node id="Expression::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_71">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_71</data>
  <data key="d2">AF(RH) = (RH/RHo)^A</data>
  <data key="d5">AF(RH) = (RH/RHo)^A</data>
  <data key="d6">Peck model for acceleration factor due to relative humidity.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_71">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_71</data>
  <data key="d2">p. 4, Eq 1</data>
  <data key="d7">In many applications, the Peck model (Escobar and Meeker, 2006) is used which is expressed as: AF(RH) = (RH/RHo)^A</data>
  <data key="d8">p. 4, Eq 1</data>
</node>
<node id="Expression::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_72">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_72</data>
  <data key="d2">AF(RH) = [RH(1-RHo)]^A / [RHo(1-RH)]^A</data>
  <data key="d5">AF(RH) = [RH(1-RHo)]^A / [RHo(1-RH)]^A</data>
  <data key="d6">Klinger model for acceleration factor due to relative humidity.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_72">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_72</data>
  <data key="d2">p. 4, Eq 2</data>
  <data key="d7">Klinger (2010) replaces RH with RH/(1-RH), and the above model is changed to</data>
  <data key="d8">p. 4, Eq 2</data>
</node>
<node id="Expression::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_73">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_73</data>
  <data key="d2">AF(RH) = \exp\{A (RH – RH0)\}</data>
  <data key="d5">AF(RH) = \exp\{A (RH – RH0)\}</data>
  <data key="d6">Exponential model for acceleration factor due to relative humidity.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_73">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::ev_73</data>
  <data key="d2">p. 4, Eq 3</data>
  <data key="d7">the acceleration effect of relative humidity can also be described by the exponential model proposed by Vernon (1927) as AF(RH) = exp{A (RH – RH0)}</data>
  <data key="d8">p. 4, Eq 3</data>
</node>
<node id="Expression::10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_74">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1515/corrrev-2019-0100::expr_74</data>
  <data key="d2">C = a + b SO_2 + c \cdot Cl + d \cdot TOW</data>
