  <data key="d2">N/A</data>
  <data key="d6">The paper qualitatively discusses the combined effect of 'high chloride ion content and high relative humidity' in marine environments leading to transition behavior in corrosion kinetics. However, no explicit mathematical coupling term is provided.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::Corrosion Science 52 (2010) 1796-1800::ev_cpl_938254801">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">Corrosion Science 52 (2010) 1796-1800::ev_cpl_938254801</data>
  <data key="d2">Abstract</data>
  <data key="d7">The atmospheric corrosion kinetics of low carbon steel exposed for up to 36 months in marine and industrial sites was studied by weight loss measurements. The results show that the mechanism and kinetics of the atmospheric corrosion process presents transition behaviour in marine environments with high chloride ion content and high relative humidity...</data>
  <data key="d8">Abstract</data>
</node>
