<node id="Coupling::maco.202414606::cpl_760599343">
  <data key="d0">Coupling</data>
  <data key="d1">maco.202414606::cpl_760599343</data>
  <data key="d2">NaCl concentration and transition phase duration</data>
  <data key="d6">A synergistic relationship exists between chloride concentration and transition phase duration, where a more concentrated salt solution accelerates corrosion with longer transition phases but decelerates it with shorter transitions. Conversely, prolonged transition phases decelerate corrosion with less chloride but accelerate it with higher chloride loads.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::maco.202414606::ev_cpl_779693251">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">maco.202414606::ev_cpl_779693251</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 14, Section 4.3</data>
  <data key="d7">During the verification tests, the synergic relationship between the two factors was revealed. The application of a more concentrated salt solution led to an acceleration of corrosion during the test with longer transition phases and to deceleration during the test with shorter transitions (Figure 10).</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 14, Section 4.3</data>
</node>
<node id="Coupling::maco.202414606::cpl_998404729">
  <data key="d0">Coupling</data>
  <data key="d1">maco.202414606::cpl_998404729</data>
  <data key="d2">wet/dry phases, temperature, and chloride supply</data>
  <data key="d6">Repeated exposure to long wet and dry phases under increased temperature intensified corrosion under a fresh supply of chlorides.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::maco.202414606::ev_cpl_291183726">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">maco.202414606::ev_cpl_291183726</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 20, Section 4.6</data>
  <data key="d7">Altogether, repeated exposure to long wet and dry phases under increased temperature intensified corrosion under a fresh supply of chlorides.</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 20, Section 4.6</data>
</node>
<node id="Coupling::maco.202414606::cpl_620739270">
  <data key="d0">Coupling</data>
  <data key="d1">maco.202414606::cpl_620739270</data>
  <data key="d2">temperature, RH, and rate of climatic change</data>
  <data key="d6">All cycling parameters, including the temperature and RH of each phase and the rate of climatic change between the particular phases, significantly affect the results and the corrosion mechanism.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::maco.202414606::ev_cpl_40210343">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
