  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1002/maco.202414745::expr_129</data>
  <data key="d2">iloc,cat = io,cat * [1 - (iloc,cat / ilim)] * exp(α*F*η / (R*T))</data>
  <data key="d5">iloc,cat = io,cat * [1 - (iloc,cat / ilim)] * exp(α*F*η / (R*T))</data>
  <data key="d6">Electrode kinetic equation for the cathodic surface, based on the Nernst diffusion layer model and the cathodic Tafel equation. Temperature (T) is a key parameter influencing the reaction rate.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::10.1002/maco.202414745::ev_129">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1002/maco.202414745::ev_129</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 4, Equation (4)</data>
  <data key="d7">Applying the Nernst diffusion layer model and the solution of the cathodic Tafel equation yields the electrode kinetic equation for the cathodic surface as</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 4, Equation (4)</data>
</node>
<node id="Expression::10.1002/maco.202414745::expr_130">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1002/maco.202414745::expr_130</data>
  <data key="d2">iloc,an = io,an * [exp(α*F*η / (R*T)) - exp(-α*F*η / (R*T))]</data>
  <data key="d5">iloc,an = io,an * [exp(α*F*η / (R*T)) - exp(-α*F*η / (R*T))]</data>
  <data key="d6">Butler-Volmer equation describing the electrode kinetics at the anode surface, where the reaction rate is dependent on temperature (T).</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::10.1002/maco.202414745::ev_130">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">10.1002/maco.202414745::ev_130</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 4, Equation (5)</data>
  <data key="d7">the Butler-Volmer equation is applied to describe the electrode kinetics at the anode surface, as shown in Equation (5)</data>
