<node id="Expression::Corrosion Science 253 (2025) 112989::expr_132">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">Corrosion Science 253 (2025) 112989::expr_132</data>
  <data key="d2">AW = AN^n</data>
  <data key="d5">AW = AN^n</data>
  <data key="d6">Empirical equation for corrosion kinetics in atmospheric conditions, relating weight gain to the number of corrosion cycles.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::Corrosion Science 253 (2025) 112989::ev_132">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">Corrosion Science 253 (2025) 112989::ev_132</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 5, Section 3.3, Equation (1)</data>
  <data key="d7">the corrosion kinetics of steel in atmospheric conditions has been shown to adhere to an empirical equation: AW = AN^n</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 5, Section 3.3, Equation (1)</data>
</node>
<node id="Expression::Corrosion Science 253 (2025) 112989::expr_133">
  <data key="d0">Expression</data>
  <data key="d1">Corrosion Science 253 (2025) 112989::expr_133</data>
  <data key="d2">log AW = log A + n log N</data>
  <data key="d5">log AW = log A + n log N</data>
  <data key="d6">Logarithmic form of the empirical corrosion kinetics equation, known as the bilogarithmic law, used to evaluate the atmospheric corrosion behavior.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::Corrosion Science 253 (2025) 112989::ev_133">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">Corrosion Science 253 (2025) 112989::ev_133</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 5, Section 3.3, Equation (2)</data>
  <data key="d7">Eq. (1) is frequently transformed into its logarithmic form, known as the bilogarithmic law... which can be expressed as: log AW = log A + n log N</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 5, Section 3.3, Equation (2)</data>
</node>
