<node id="Coupling::Popova_2025_Effect_of_Drying_on_Corrosion::cpl_617650103">
  <data key="d0">Coupling</data>
  <data key="d1">Popova_2025_Effect_of_Drying_on_Corrosion::cpl_617650103</data>
  <data key="d2">RH influences electrolyte evaporation, which in turn influences chloride concentration and oxygen diffusion path.</data>
  <data key="d6">Coupling between relative humidity (RH) and chloride concentration/oxygen diffusion path.</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::Popova_2025_Effect_of_Drying_on_Corrosion::ev_cpl_832723581">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">Popova_2025_Effect_of_Drying_on_Corrosion::ev_cpl_832723581</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 2, Paragraph 1</data>
  <data key="d7">During subsequent drying, the RH decreases, the electrolyte evaporates, the concentration of dissolved species increases and the oxygen diffusion path through the thin electrolyte film to the corroding surface is shorter, resulting in an increase in the corrosion aggressiveness [10, 11, 13-17].</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 2, Paragraph 1</data>
</node>
<node id="Coupling::Popova_2025_Effect_of_Drying_on_Corrosion::cpl_556125039">
