  <data key="d2">C = Kt^n</data>
  <data key="d5">C = Kt^n</data>
  <data key="d6">General empirical equation describing the variation of corrosion loss (C) with time (t).</data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence::Kinetics of atmospheric corrosion of mild steel, zinc, galvanized iron and aluminium at 10 exposure stations in India::ev_190">
  <data key="d0">Evidence</data>
  <data key="d1">Kinetics of atmospheric corrosion of mild steel, zinc, galvanized iron and aluminium at 10 exposure stations in India::ev_190</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 4, Eq. (1)</data>
  <data key="d7">The variation of weight loss (C) due to corrosion expressed as micrometres (µm) with time (t) can be described by the general empirical equation in the form C = Kt^n</data>
  <data key="d8">Page 4, Eq. (1)</data>
</node>
<node id="Expression::Kinetics of atmospheric corrosion of mild steel, zinc, galvanized iron and aluminium at 10 exposure stations in India::expr_191">
